INT. ZERO-G LAUNDROMAT - ORBITAL HAB RING - NIGHT CYCLE

Washers hum on the walls like nesting beetles. Clothes float in soapy spheres.

TANVEER and MBALI float by the dryers, arguing in whispers. She jabs a finger at his chest. He catches it, gently. OSKAR clings to a handrail, pale, a laundry bag knotted around his wrist.

LIN drifts up from the aft hatch, holding a wrench, and cuts the whisper in half with her voice.

LIN
Who ran a wash with coolant in it?

Nobody answers. She turns slowly in the air. They all look at Oskar.

OSKAR
It was a blue bottle.

LIN
It was coolant.

DOC FENWICK, an old man in a cardigan, pushes off the far wall like a swimmer and catches a floating sock. He examines it, sniffs it, and sighs.

DOC FENWICK
Everybody out.

RHEA, the youngest, laughs, then stops, then laughs harder. The washer behind her shudders. A warning light goes from green to red. Mbali grabs Tanveer. Lin grabs Oskar. Doc Fenwick grabs the sock. The machine bursts open and a pink cloud of foam rolls across the room, swallowing all six of them.
